 {"status": "complete", "id": "INT-GL-2", "title": "P2 \u2014 gitreins judge tier1 secrets cell cannot pass on this repo: .gitleaks.toml excludes harness state (.gitreins/**) and the judge grades that exclusion as a FAIL, so every verdict reads Overall FAIL even when tier2 PASS", "detail": {"fingerprint": "2db0aa1bb822a811bd589b623bd130bb577cafcd96768f6f76f2b9220696234a"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "MEASURED on two consecutive judge runs, both reporting Overall FAIL while their tier2 stage PASSed. (1) 2026-10-27 verdict a6cee00a (task DF-AIPP-17): '~ secrets: Command timed out after 120s (step budget)'. (2) 2026-10-28 verdict dir .gitreins/history/2026-10-28/fdc2374b (task INT-CI-2): '\u2717 secrets: harness state excluded from gitleaks scope (.gitreins/**)', with stages.tier1.passed=false / any_failed=true and stages.tier2.passed=true (criterion reported COMPLETE with the bug reproduced and the fix verified). So the repo's verdict signal is degraded: a fully verified tier2 delivery is indistinguishable from a failed one at the Overall line. NOT a leak: independent gitleaks detect over the full history (1382 commits, ~49.5MB) reports 'no leaks found', and the commit-time pre-commit guard reported 'secrets \u2014 clean (gitleaks + builtin cross-check)' on the same tree. CAUSE: .gitleaks.toml [allowlist].paths carries '''.gitreins/''' and '''.gitreins/history/''', added under INT-GL-1 so the full-tree scan would stop grading untracked harness state and scan logs; the judge's tier1 secrets step now treats the resulting scope exclusion as a non-pass rather than a benign skip. SAME FAMILY as GUARD-1 (a gate whose verdict is decided by something other than the property it claims to measure). Fix direction (decide, do not guess): (a) narrow the allowlist to the harness subpaths that actually trip false positives (logs/history) so the declared scope is complete, (b) teach the guard to treat an allowlisted-scope exclusion as a benign skip (allow_skips is already true for the benign empty-scope case), or (c) drop the .gitreins entries and pin the false-positive text itself. Whichever is chosen, tier1 must go back to reporting PASS when lint and tests pass. RE-MEASURED 2026-10-30 (PM tick ai-plays-poke-pm-2026-10-30-17-26-12): premise LIVE - 2026-10-29 verdicts 4456816d, 673b09fd, c09d246d still emit '\u2717 secrets: harness state excluded from gitleaks scope (.gitreins/**)' with stages.tier1.passed=false, and 91993654/97d4475f time out in the secrets cell at the 120s step budget (same timeout family as a6cee00a). SECOND CONTRIBUTOR, measured in fdc2374b (2026-10-28) secrets step output: the builtin cross-check also reports 'Secrets scan: 1 potential findings' - '.env.example: SENSITIVE PATH (credential-store path class) \u2014 staging this file is blocked regardless of content', with 'secrets: builtin cross-check status: 1 finding' and exit_code 1. Fixing only the .gitreins allowlist (options a/b/c) will NOT make acceptance criterion 1 pass; the chosen option must ALSO resolve, or record an explicit justified override for, the .env.example builtin finding - otherwise the secrets cell keeps failing for this second reason the original diagnosis did not name.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "1) A judge run on this repo with lint and tests passing reports stages.tier1.passed == true, and the secrets cell is a PASS (or an explicitly benign skip) \u2014 it no longer emits the 'harness state excluded from gitleaks scope (.gitreins/**)' FAIL. 2) Verify on the exact artifact: python3 -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('.gitreins/history/<date>/<dir>/verdict.json'));print(d['stages']['tier1']['passed'])\" prints True for a run whose lint and tests cells passed. 3) No new false positives are introduced: gitleaks detect over the full tree/history still reports 'no leaks found' and the commit-time guard still prints 'secrets \u2014 clean'. 4) The chosen option is recorded in the row with its rationale (allowlist narrowing vs benign-skip classification vs FP pinning), because .gitreins/** contains scanner logs whose text is what tripped the original INT-GL-1 false positives.", "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-10-28T02:38:49.203003+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-30 18:02:43", "completed_at": "2026-10-30 18:02:43", "worker_status": "complete", "foreman_note": "INT-GL-2 CLOSED 2026-10-30 (option (a): narrow the allowlist \u2014 narrowed to empty, because measurement shows nothing under .gitreins/ trips a rule \u2014 PLUS the .env.example sensitive-path override, which is the actual blocker). RE-DIAGNOSIS, measured not assumed: the 'harness state excluded from gitleaks scope (.gitreins/**)' line was NEVER the failure cause. It is an unconditional informational echo that the tier1 secrets step prints as its FIRST output line (gitreins engine/pipeline.py tier1 secrets step), and the verdict summary renders output[0] after the marker \u2014 so every secrets failure is displayed as if the exclusion were the cause. Proof it is not a FAIL trigger: verdict 2026-10-18/f15b8199 records that same line with '\u2713 secrets' and stages.tier1.passed=true. The real exit-1 in the four failing 2026-10-28/29 verdicts (fdc2374b, b21e1430, a893f872, 4456816d, 673b09fd, c09d246d) is the builtin cross-check's '.env.example: SENSITIVE PATH (credential-store path class)' finding, data.exit_code=1. Second reason the .gitreins entries could not be the cause: the judge renders its OWN gitleaks config (engine.guard_manager.harness_scan_gitleaks_config) which always allowlists HARNESS_STATE_DIRS=('.gitreins',), and the builtin skips _is_harness_state_path() unconditionally \u2014 so .gitreins/** is out of scope with or without the repo entries. WHAT CHANGED: (1) .gitleaks.toml \u2014 removed '''.gitreins/''' and '''.gitreins/history/'''. Narrowing decision is measured: with both entries deleted, gitleaks detect --no-git (the scan mode the guard uses) is CLEAN over 27,665,541 bytes in the worktree and 407,784,243 bytes in the main clone (incl. 17MB history + 8.7MB guard logs), and --no-git OFF is clean over the full 1423-commit history. Nothing under .gitreins/ trips a pattern today, so there is no subpath to narrow to and no FP text to pin (option (c) would have nothing to pin); the declared scope is now the complete tree, and the repo config no longer carries a blanket dir exclusion that reads as the reason a secrets cell failed. Residual risk accepted and named: if a future verdict/patch/guard-log ever quotes real leaked text under .gitreins/, that is a TRUE positive in a tracked file and must be caught, not excluded. (2) .gitreins/config.yaml \u2014 guards.sensitive_paths.allow: ['.env.example']. This is the documented REVIEW-GITREINS-027 knob and the ONLY one that works: the path class is evaluated BEFORE the .gitleaks.toml allowlist by design ('an allowlist path may exempt content findings, but it must NOT silence the path class'), and tests/test_secrets_allowlist.py::test_unrelated_sources_are_still_scanned explicitly asserts .env.example is NOT in the gitleaks allowlist. Justification: .env.example is a tracked TEMPLATE whose two values are word-shaped placeholders (30 and 25 chars shaped 'xx-xx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxx-xxx-xxxx' \u2014 no high-entropy run, never live keys); the finding is a false positive by design, and the override is not silent: the cell now carries 'sensitive-path override applied: .env.example'. VERIFIED: exact judge step command regenerated from the live tier1 plan (engine.pipeline.tier1_plan) in this worktree and replayed \u2014 exit 0, 'secrets: gitleaks: clean' + 'builtin cross-check status: clean' + the override note; the same cell A/B'd in-process (config with the override stripped = exit 1 and the .env.example finding, with it = exit 0). Regression: gitleaks detect --no-banner clean both modes, ruff clean, mypy 0 errors, tests/test_secrets_allowlist.py + tests/test_precommit_hook.py 15/15 pass. UPSTREAM (filed, not fixed here \u2014 it lives in ~/gitreins, not this repo): the tier1 secrets step should not echo the harness-state scope line BEFORE the scanner outcomes; because it does, verdict summaries misattribute every secrets failure to the scope exclusion (this row and INT-GL-1's follow-up were both misdiagnosed on exactly that line). RESIDUAL NOT CLOSED BY THIS ROW: verdicts 2026-10-29/91993654 and 97d4475f failed the same cell with data.timed_out=true/timeout_s=120 and EMPTY output \u2014 a fleet-load timeout on a 384MB whole-tree scan whose nominal cost is 16.3s. That is a separate capacity/scope row, not an allowlist defect, and AC1/AC2 (a verdict artifact with tier1.passed=true) still require a full judge run on the merged tree \u2014 this worktree ships no venv, so the tests cell skips here.", "evidence": "Judge-step replay in this worktree (command regenerated from engine.pipeline.tier1_plan): exit 0 / 'secrets: gitleaks: clean' / 'builtin cross-check status: clean' / 'sensitive-path override applied: .env.example'. In-process A/B on the same cell (guards.sensitive_paths stripped): exit 1 + '.env.example: SENSITIVE PATH (credential-store path class)'; with it: exit 0. gitleaks detect --no-git clean at 27,665,541 B (worktree) and 407,784,243 B (main clone) with the .gitreins entries removed; --no-git OFF clean over 1423 commits / 53,176,593 B. ruff: All checks passed. mypy src/: Success, 69 files. pytest tests/test_secrets_allowlist.py tests/test_precommit_hook.py: 15 passed. Baseline FAIL verdicts inspected: .gitreins/history/2026-10-29/4456816d, 673b09fd, c09d246d (secrets exit_code=1), 91993654, 97d4475f (timed_out=true, timeout_s=120), 2026-10-28/fdc2374b, b21e1430, a893f872; PASSING control with the same scope line: .gitreins/history/2026-10-18/f15b8199 (tier1.passed=true).", "capability_tags": ["gitreins", "gitleaks", "guard", "verdict-signal"], "commit_hash": "1003011", "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worker_summary": "Tier1 secrets cell: narrowed .gitleaks.toml (dropped the two broad .gitreins/ entries after proving both trees scan clean without them) and cleared the real blocker with the documented guards.sensitive_paths.allow override for the tracked .env.example template; the judge's exact secrets step now exits 0 with an auditable 'sensitive-path override applied' note.", "files_changed": [".gitleaks.toml", ".gitreins/config.yaml"]}
