 {"id": "ARM-2", "title": "[P1] decision modes: JEV, LLM, and both together \u2014 selectable at runtime with a pluggable model per mode", "status": "complete", "priority": "P1", "complexity": "4", "depends_on": [], "blocks": [], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "Bane 2026-10-29: JEV and the LLM are supposed to work TOGETHER, and the choice is a MODE, not a shipped default - allow different LLMs, JEV on or JEV off. This replaces the ARM-1 question of which arm to ship. Current state is wrong in two ways: DEFAULT_DECISION_MODE is hardcoded to jev, and the jev-only arm measured 0/5 at leaving Pallet Town while pure-LLM did 6/6, so the hardcoded default is the worst available choice. Required: (1) decision_mode selectable as jev | llm | hybrid, where hybrid is the shipped intent - JEV answers every cycle and hands back to the LLM when it self-reports uncertainty; (2) model+provider selectable per mode rather than global; (3) existing jev/llm spellings keep producing byte-identical decision_mode values so prior episode logs stay comparable (M6 back-compat); (4) nothing is hardcoded as a default arm.", "acceptance": "1) A mode selector exists reachable from config/env/CLI and setting it to jev, llm, or hybrid produces that decision_mode in the episode log. 2) A run in each of the three modes completes and records its mode. 3) The same model+provider can be set per mode independently and is read back from the episode log. 4) grep shows no hardcoded DEFAULT_DECISION_MODE fallback arm. 5) A focused test covers mode parsing plus back-compat for the legacy jev/llm strings.", "worker_status": "complete", "completed_at": "2026-10-29T22:25:00+00:00", "commit_hash": "979cb8850ec2b74f2c2094626d06884a12c74218", "worker_summary": "Decision modes are now runtime-selected with per-mode models and no shipped default arm. (AC1/AC2/AC5-shape already existed via b940c53: flag/env selection, decision_mode + decision_mode_family stamping, parser tests.) DELIVERED HERE: (AC3) resolve_teacher_model + --teacher-model + AIPP_TEACHER_MODEL/CRON_TEACHER_MODEL, independent of the controller model with controller fallback, threaded through both hybrid teacher call sites and stamped into decision rows and run_autonomy; (AC4) DEFAULT_DECISION_MODE deleted - git grep gives no .py hits - resolve_decision_mode returns None when nothing is chosen and main() refuses with rc=2 'decision mode is required; choose --decision-mode from system1, system2, system1+system2, hybrid, jev, llm, agentic or set AIPP_DECISION_MODE / CRON_DECISION_MODE'; (AC5) tests/test_arm2_models.py (5 tests) + updated legacy pins. Foreman-verified: missing mode rc=2, explicit --decision-mode jev --dry-run --skip-key-check rc=0, focused 59 passed, merged full suite 4570 passed 14 skipped, ruff+mypy clean, gitleaks no leaks on 0fbd009..HEAD.\nch:trace row=ARM-2 spec=.coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl#ARM-2 wave=.coding-hermes/waves/ai-plays-poke-foreman-2026-10-29-21-43-09.json#ARM-2 test=tests/test_arm2_models.py::test_teacher_model_resolution_is_flag_then_env_then_controller doc=docs/api/cron_runner.md prompt=/tmp/ai-plays-poke-foreman-2026-10-29-21-43-09-ARM-2-brief.txt evidence=8f7d86964833dd81de3ba291c9bf8be2d91ea55c witness=live:dry-run-refusal-and-jev-pass verdict=none:pending-rejudge commit=8f7d86964833dd81de3ba291c9bf8be2d91ea55c memory=/project/ai-plays-poke/ticks/ai-plays-poke-foreman-2026-10-29-21-43-09 STATUS: complete TIER: T3 EVIDENCE: 8f7d86964833dd81de3ba291c9bf8be2d91ea55c\n\nAC3 FOLLOW-UP (foreman-direct, commit 979cb8850ec2b74f2c2094626d06884a12c74218, merged 91b06d5): Tier 2 verdict 0bf69185 accepted AC4/AC5 and the trace marker but failed AC3 - the model choice was teacher-vs-controller, not keyed BY MODE, and no provider was recorded. Closed with: MODE_MODEL_ENV_VARS / MODE_PROVIDER_ENV_VARS (AIPP_|CRON_<MODE>_MODEL and _PROVIDER for system1, system2, system1+system2 - jev and hybrid both key the hybrid slot); provider_of() deriving the provider the way the client already routes (openai/ prefix, deepseek ids -> deepseek, typesafe/jev -> typesafe, else None - never invented); resolve_mode_models() returning every family's model+provider plus active_family; effective_decision_model() for the deciding arm. A per-mode pin now CHANGES the request (system2 runs use the system2 slot, hybrid runs use the hybrid slot teacher) and unset slots fall back to the controller/teacher chain, so a run that sets nothing is byte-identical (M6). The map is stamped on run_autonomy AND on every per-decision row (the episode log a benchmark reads) and printed at startup. Gates on the AC3 commit: pre-commit full guard PASS (secrets/lint/tests full/static_analysis/lsp), 4570 passed 15 skipped xdist, mypy clean on src/ and cron_runner.py, ruff check+format clean, 10 tests in tests/test_arm2_models.py.\nch:trace row=ARM-2 spec=.coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl#ARM-2 wave=.coding-hermes/waves/ai-plays-poke-foreman-2026-10-29-21-43-09.json#ARM-2 test=tests/test_arm2_models.py::test_mode_models_resolve_independently_per_mode doc=docs/api/cron_runner.md prompt=/tmp/ai-plays-poke-foreman-2026-10-29-21-43-09-ARM-2-brief.txt evidence=979cb8850ec2b74f2c2094626d06884a12c74218 witness=live:dry-run-refusal-and-jev-pass+8f7d86964833dd81de3ba291c9bf8be2d91ea55c verdict=0bf69185:ac4-ac5-pass-ac3-fail-then-closed commit=979cb8850ec2b74f2c2094626d06884a12c74218 memory=/project/ai-plays-poke/ticks/ai-plays-poke-foreman-2026-10-29-21-43-09 STATUS: complete TIER: T3 EVIDENCE: 979cb8850ec2b74f2c2094626d06884a12c74218", "foreman_note": "Owner decision 0fbd009 implemented: 'JEV and the LLM work together; the choice is a MODE, not a shipped default arm'. Wave ai-plays-poke-foreman-2026-10-29-21-43-09 (worker gpt-5.6-sol @ openai-codex, 8f7d869, merged 5dc6a0d) + foreman-direct AC3 follow-up 979cb88 (merged 91b06d5) after Tier 2 0bf69185 failed AC3 on the literal mode-keyed/provider reading. CARRIED FORWARD fo